1028 0 obj
<<
/Title (Following safety procedures before, during, and after an earthquake is essential. Secure heavy furniture, identify safe places, and practise emergency drills beforehand. During shaking, remember to **Drop, Cover, and Hold On**. Afterward, check for hazards, stay alert for aftershocks, avoid damaged buildings, and follow official safety instructions.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1021 0 R
>>
endobj
1029 0 obj
<<
/Title (Families should prepare emergency contacts, communication methods, and meeting locations. Schools should practise earthquake drills and identify evacuation routes. Communities can also support vulnerable people, keep emergency routes clear, and share reliable safety information.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1022 0 R
>>
endobj
